		<devNote>misc</devNote>
		<description>The name derives from the ancient shepherd's words "grini" (greenery, grass, and also the death rattle of a fool with a club) and "ziabr" (what he breathes and bites off limbs with). The clarification "from the word Grini" became established in folklore after seven linguists tried to out-argue GriniZiabr about declensions and were eaten along with their dictionaries.</description>
